{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"\n\nThe original `release_on_behalf_of` popped the waiter out of `_wait_queue` and set its event, but the waiter only added itself to `_borrowers` after `await event.wait()` resumed it — so between `event.set()` and that resumption, the freed token was in no bookkeeping structure: the queue was empty and `_borrowers` was under full. The `acquire_on_behalf_of_nowait` guard (`if self._wait_queue or len(self._borrowers) >= self._total_tokens`) therefore saw an empty queue and a spare slot, and admitted a second borrower for the one token that was already earmarked for the woken waiter."}}
